## Considered and not used

These were looked at and left alone, each for the reason given. Nothing from them is in this project.

- https://developer.apple.com/streaming/examples/: source: Apple sample video. SKIPPED. The examples page carries no license grant or terms for reusing the sample streams, only Apple's site-wide terms. Under the repo rule that anything unverified is dropped, we do not download it. Baseline sanity uses a locally generated ffmpeg clip instead, which has no license question at all.
- https://www.nssl.noaa.gov/news/b-roll/: source: NOAA NSSL B-roll. SKIPPED. The b-roll page serves its clips through a Vimeo showcase and exposes no direct file links, and no yt-dlp is installed on this machine. Nothing was downloaded. NOAA works are generally public domain, but we did not verify a per-clip statement, so the source is open rather than confirmed.
- https://archive.org/search?query=hell%27s+angels+1930: source: Hell's Angels (1930). SKIPPED. No copy of the 1930 film is on the Internet Archive; the hits are unrelated modern documentaries. Not downloaded. If a copy turns up, note that the repo rule keeps that title out of anything we publish because of the trademark.

